B4 is impossible. So B4 can only help B3-B4-B5 or B4-B5-B6. B3-B4-B5 is very live. Discarding B4 is risky.\n- **Play B8**: B8 is less central. Possible Chows: B6-B7-B8, B7-B8-B9. B7 has 1 left, B9 has 1 left \u2014 both low availability. So B8 is relatively safe. Also, we only have one B8, and no supporting tiles. Least dangerous discard.\n\nNow consider scoring potential:  \nWe have:\n- Pung of W3 (terminal/honor? No \u2014 W3 is wind, honor tile) \u2192 F3 is West Wind. W3 is Character-3, not a wind. Mistake!\n\nWait: **F3 is West Wind**, but **W3 is Character-3** (suit tile). So [W3,W3,W3] is a pung of Character-3, a simple suited tile.\n\nOur melds:\n- [W3,W3,W3]: pung of W3 (Characters)\n- [W5,W6,W7]: chow\n\nOther players' melds:\n- Next: [W2,W2,W2] \u2192 W2 pung\n- Across: [J3,J3,J3] \u2192 White Dragon\n- Previous: [F1,F1,F1] \u2192 East Wind\n\nPrevailing Wind: West (F3), Seat Wind: West (F3)\n\nSo we do **not** have a wind pung \u2014 we have W3 (Character-3), not F3 (West Wind). So no Prevalent/Seat Wind benefit yet.\n\nOur hand: W6, T4x2, B3, B4x2, B5, B8\n\nPossible shape: trying to build more chows in Bamboos? B3-B4-B5 is a natural chow draw. We could aim for Pure Straight (16 pts): need 1-2-3, 4-5-6, 7-8-9 in same suit. But we have B3,B4,B5 \u2014 that's 3-4-5, not a full straight.\n\nAlternatively, All Simples (2 pts) if we avoid terminals and honors \u2014 currently all our tiles are simples (2-8 suited), except possibly melds: W3 is terminal? No \u2014 W3 is 3-character, which is **not** terminal. Terminals are 1 and 9. So W3 is simple. So [W3,W3,W3] is a pung of simples.\n\nOur entire hand and melds: all simples! W3, W5-W6-W7, and current hand: W6, T4, B3, B4, B5, B8 \u2014 all simples. So if we win with self-draw and concealed hand, we can get **All Simples (2 pts)** + possibly **Fully Concealed Hand (4 pts)** or **Self Drawn (1 pt)**.\n\nBut we have an exposed Peng (W3) and Chi (W5-W6-W7), so **not concealed**. Melded Hand pattern applies (all 