ngs, two chows, pair T8\n- No honor tiles \u2192 No Honors: 1 point\n- Self Drawn: 1 point (if I draw it)\n- All Simples? T8 is simple (not 1 or 9), W3 is terminal? W3 is 3 \u2014 not terminal. Terminal is 1 or 9. W3 is simple. T4 is simple. So all tiles are simples \u2192 All Simples: 2 points\n- So minimum: No Honors (1) + All Simples (2) + Self Drawn (1) = 4 points \u2014 still not enough.\n\nBut if I have a pung of seat wind? Seat wind is West (F3) \u2014 I don\u2019t have it, and F3 is all discarded.\n\nDragon? No.\n\nMixed Shifted Chows? My chows: W5-6-7 and B3-4-5 \u2014 different suits, not consecutive numbers.\n\nNo obvious high-scoring pattern.\n\nBut wait: I have **two pungs**: W3 and T4 \u2014 different suits, different numbers.\n\nBut if I could get a third pung, and shift to All Pungs (6 points), plus All Simples (2), No Honors (1), Self Drawn (1) \u2192 total 10 \u2014 qualifies.\n\nBut I already have two pungs and two chows \u2014 I cannot convert chows into pungs.\n\nUnless I break a chow \u2014 but I can't.\n\nSo stuck with two chows and two pungs.\n\nThus, **cannot achieve All Pungs or All Chows**.\n\nMaximum possible fans:\n- No Honors: 1\n- All Simples: 2 (since no 1,9 or honors)\n- Self Drawn: 1\n- Possibly Single Wait: if I am waiting only for one tile type (e.g., only T8), and it completes the pair, and no other winning possibility \u2192 1 point\n- But Edge Wait, Closed Wait: only for chows \u2014 I\u2019m completing pair, so Single Wait applies\n\nSo maximum: 1+2+1+1 = 5 points \u2014 still less than 8.\n\nWait \u2014 is that possible? Am I stuck with a losing hand?\n\nBut perhaps I missed something.\n\nWait: **All Simples requires no terminals and no honors** \u2014 terminals are 1 and 9.\n\nDo I have any terminal?\n\n- W3: 3 \u2014 ok\n- T4: 4 \u2014 ok\n- W5-6-7: 5,6,7 \u2014 ok\n- B3-4-5: 3,4,5 \u2014 ok\n- Pair: if W6 or T8 \u2014 both simples\n\nYes \u2014 all tiles are 2-8, no 1 or 9, no honors \u2192 All Simples: 2 points\n\nNo Honors: 1 point\n\nSelf Drawn: 1 point\n\nSingle Wait: 1 point (if only one way to win)\n\nTotal: 5 points \u2014 insufficient.\n\nBut wait \u2014 **do I have a pung of simples? Yes \u2014 W3 and T4 are both simples**.\n\nBut no additional pattern.\n\nIs there a possibility of **Mixed Double Pung**? Only if two pungs of same number \u2014 W3 and T4 are different numbers.\n\nNo.\n\nBut wait \u2014 **Triple Pung**? Three pungs of same number \u2014 no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can win by **Last Tile Claim** or **Robbing Kong**, but those depend on others.\n\nBut under normal rules, I must have at least 8 points.\n\nThis suggests my current hand **cannot win legally**, because even if completed, it scores only 5 points max.\n\nBut that can't be right \u2014 perhaps I miscalculated.\n\nWait: **are there any concealed kongs or pungs?**\n\nMy pungs are both exposed: Peng W3, Peng T4 \u2014 so not concealed.\n\nChows are exposed.\n\nSo no Fully Concealed Hand.\n\nAnother idea: **did I form a kong?**\n\nThe meld [T4, T4, T4] \u2014 is it a kong? No, only three tiles \u2014 so pung.\n\nBut in history: after Peng T4, did I promote? No BuGang recorded.\n\nSimilarly, no other kong.\n\nBut look at across player: they Gang T5 \u2014 so T5 is fully used.\n\nNow, back to problem: my hand seems to be a **Chicken Hand**, worth 0 fans \u2014 but with All Simples (2), No Honors (1), Self Drawn (1), Single Wait (1) \u2014 still 5.\n\nBut **Chicken Hand pattern is worth 8 points** \u2014 defined as a hand otherwise worth zero fans, but wins anyway.\n\nAh! This is key.\n\nFrom the description:\n> * Chicken Hand: A hand which would otherwise be worth of zero fans, with flower tiles not included.\n\nSo if my hand has **some fans**, I cannot use Chicken Hand.\n\nBut if I have **zero fans**, then Chicken Hand gives me 8.\n\nBut here, I have **at least 3 fans**: All Simples (2), No Honors (1) \u2014 minimum 3.\n\nSo I cannot claim Chicken Hand.\n\nThus, I **must** reach 8 points through other combinations.\n\nBut with two chows and two pungs, all exposed, no honors, all simples \u2014 what fans can I get?\n\nLet\u2019s list all possible fans I might have upon winning:\n\n1. All Simples: 2 points \u2014 yes\n2. No Honors: 1 point \u2014 yes\n3. Self Drawn: 1 point \u2014 if I draw it\n4. Single Wait: 1 point \u2014 if only one tile completes the win\n5. Mixed Double Pung: 2 points \u2014 if I have two pungs of same number \u2014 but W3 and T4 are different\n6. Two Concealed Pungs: 2 points \u2014 but both pungs are exposed (Peng) \u2014 no\n7. Melded Kong: 2 points \u2014 if I have an exposed kong \u2014 but I don\u2019t\n8. Pung of Terminals or Honors: 1 point \u2014 but W3 and T4 are simples \u2014 not terminals or honors \u2014 so no\n9. One Voided Suit: 1 point \u2014 but I have W, T, B \u2014 three suits \u2014 no\n10. All Chows: 2 points \u2014 no, I have pungs\n11. All Pungs: 6 points \u2014 no, I have chows\n\nNone of the 6-point or above patterns apply.\n\nClosest: All Pungs is 6, but I have chows.\n\nSo it seems **my hand cannot reach 8 points**.\n\nBut that suggests I should never have made those Pengs \u2014 but I did.\n\nPerhaps I misread the melds.\n\nWait: the system says \"Your melds are: [[W3, W3, W3],[W5, W6, W7],[T4, T4, T4],[B3, B4, B5]]\"\n\n[W5, W6, W7] is a chow, [B3, B4, B5] is a chow.\n\nTwo chows, two pungs.\n\nNo way to remove them.\n\nUnless... is there a possibility that [W5, W6, W7] is not a chow but part of something else? No.\n\nPerhaps the game allows winning with less than 8 points in special cases \u2014 but per rules, no.\n\nAnother possibility: **Out With Replacement Tile** \u2014 if I make a kong and draw replacement, then win \u2014 8 points.\n\nBut I have no kong, and no fourth copy to promote.\n\nFor example, I have T4 pung \u2014 are there T4 left? Unshown T4: 0 \u2014 all four are used: I have three, and one was discarded? History: I Peng\u2019d T4 \u2014 so I took it from discard. Total four T4 \u2014 all accounted